  "body": "Follow-up from #786, part of #131.\n\n**What happens today:** #786 made `spindle.rigid_tapping` a validated `.mch` capability, and the program gate refuses tap cycles by name on any machine that states `false`. Every Tormach mill and router file states it. The three Tormach lathe files (`tormach-8l.mch`, `tormach-15l-slant-pro.mch`, `tormach-15lx-slant-pro.mch`) don't state it, so they read as \"not limited\". The public material found during #786 didn't settle whether these lathes rigid-tap: PathPilot release notes mention a G84 tapping cycle but don't tie it to a lathe model and spindle.\n\n**Expected:** each Tormach lathe file states `rigid_tapping` as its operator manual documents it (behaviour only, clean room), with the source cited in a `docs/decisions/` entry. If the manuals still don't settle it, say so on this issue and leave the files unstated.\n\n**Done means:**\n- The 8L, 15L Slant-PRO and 15LX Slant-PRO files each state `rigid_tapping` from a cited public source, or this issue records why they can't.\n- `every_tormach_mill_and_router_file_states_rigid_tapping` in `crates/app/tests/rigid_tapping.rs` is widened to cover the lathes.\n\nEffort: high, under the safety floor (it decides whether a G84 is posted).\n",
